version 0.17.0
component cap-tantalum-7343

# A polarised tantalum capacitor, stated as a class: the capacitance, the tolerance and the working
# voltage it has to take. Which part is bought for it is a procurement decision, not a fact of the
# class.
#
# The polarity is a fact of the class, not a hint in the file name: pin 1 is the positive pole and
# pin 2 the negative one, so the two pins are typed `polarized` and `positive_pin 1` says which of
# them is the positive one (ADR-0078). The requirement is then read in that direction — the forward
# stress across the two poles — instead of as a magnitude across the part's two pins.

kind         generic
category     capacitor
construction tantalum
polarized    yes
positive_pin  1

symbol passives:c-pol
footprint tantalum:tantalum-7343
params
  value      capacitance required
  tolerance  percent     required
  voltage    voltage     required
  esr        resistance  optional

pins
  1  P  polarized
  2  N  polarized
